      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>The Regulatory Reform (Fire Safety) Order 2005 says keep fire doors in effective working order.</li><li>The Fire Safety (England) Regulations 2022 say check common fire doors every three months in homes of four or more storeys. They have applied since January 2023.</li><li>The Building Safety Act 2022 covers higher-risk buildings: 18 metres or seven storeys, with two or more homes.</li><li>Check the leaf, frame, seals, hinges, closer, signs, glass and gaps.</li><li>A check with no record gives you no protection.</li></ul>"
