      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The law",
      "heading": "Three laws set your duty.",
      "html": "<p>The <strong>Regulatory Reform (Fire Safety) Order 2005</strong> covers all non-domestic buildings and the shared parts of homes. Article 17 says keep fire protection, including fire doors, in good working order. It gives no set number of checks. So check often and write it down.</p><p>The <strong>Fire Safety (England) Regulations 2022</strong> cover homes of four or more storeys. Check shared fire doors every three months. Check flat entrance doors every year.</p><p>The <strong>Building Safety Act 2022</strong> covers higher-risk buildings. These are 18 metres or seven storeys, with two or more homes. Failures can be a personal liability.</p>"
